+<!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->
+## What Was Built
+
+Five research iterations, one open item each, ending in a single recommendation with its cost
+and blast radius rather than a survey. Nothing in the shipped system changed; this phase is
+evidence and a decision set.
+
+### Phase 1: open-items-research
+
+The run measured line width across the whole corpus, re-verified every unowned surface against
+the current tree, checked each claim in the root README goal section against the code, counted
+what a rename of the colliding manifest name would touch, and prototyped each candidate machine
+check before recommending it.
+
+It found one defect nobody had reported: three environment variables the OpenCode plugin reads
+by name appear in neither `.env.example` nor the plugin's own table, so an operator can set them
+but cannot discover them. Confirmed independently before this summary was written.
+
+It also answered a question the strategy worded ambiguously. The strategy's line-width figure was
+measured over four JavaScript files against the JavaScript style guide; the run read "goal files"
+as markdown and answered about prose. Its prose conclusion is sound and its code measurement
+stands, but the two are not the same question, and the record says so rather than quietly
+adopting the substitution.
+
